  "version": "1.0",
  "written_before_scoring": true,
  "matching": "spaCy lemmas, lower-case, alphabetic tokens; multi-word terms are matched as consecutive lemmas",
  "design_notes": [
    "Each term belongs to exactly one frame, so one word can never count twice.",
    "Topic-defining words are left out because they occur in almost every text about AI regulation and would swamp the regulation/governance frame: regulate, regulation, rule, law, government, policy, AI, artificial intelligence. That frame is represented by institutions and mechanisms (regulator, oversight, enforcement, compliance, audit...).",
    "Very general words are left out because they fit several frames: trust, ethical, protect, fair (alone), growth, development, public, society.",
    "Frames are counted by emphasis, not by stance: 'stifle innovation' counts towards innovation/opportunity because the text is talking about innovation.",
    "Prompts contain some of these words (safety testing, personal data, facial recognition, false information). Chatbot answers echo them. This is checked separately in a robustness run that ignores terms present in the answer's own prompt.",
    "Removed as too ambiguous in news text: report, fine, monitor, tracking, capital."
  ],
